<title>FRANCE: Dassault signs Polish cooperation deal.</title>
<headline>Dassault signs Polish cooperation deal.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French combat plane maker Dassault Aviation said on Friday it has signed a letter of intent with WSK PZL-Mielec of Poland for industrial cooperation tied to any acquisition of its Mirage 2000-5 fighter-bomber by the Polish government.</p>
<p>The agreement allows final assembly of the aircraft in Poland and manufacture of airframe parts and sub-assemblies. Training and support are also covered by the agreement.</p>
<p>Dassault will also develop broader areas of aeronautical cooperation and projects to boost the local economy, the company said in a statement at the air show here.</p>
</text>
